<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Network Anomaly Detection System Report</title>
    <style>
        @page {
            size: A4;
            margin: 20mm;
        }

        body {
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
            color: #2d3748;
            line-height: 1.6;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 24px;
            background-color: #ffffff;
        }

        .header {
            border-bottom: 2px solid #e2e8f0;
            padding-bottom: 16px;
            margin-bottom: 28px;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 24px;
            color: #0f172a;
            margin: 0 0 6px 0;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: -0.5px;
        }

        .subtitle {
            font-size: 14px;
            color: #64748b;
            margin: 0;
        }

        .meta-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
            gap: 12px;
            background-color: #f8fafc;
            border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
            border-radius: 6px;
            padding: 14px 18px;
            margin-bottom: 28px;
            font-size: 13px;
        }

        .meta-item {
            color: #475569;
        }

        .meta-item strong {
            color: #0f172a;
        }

        h2 {
            font-size: 16px;
            color: #0f172a;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
            padding-bottom: 6px;
            margin-top: 24px;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.5px;
        }

        p {
            font-size: 13.5px;
            margin-top: 0;
            margin-bottom: 14px;
            color: #334155;
        }

        ul {
            margin: 0 0 16px 0;
            padding-left: 20px;
            font-size: 13.5px;
            color: #334155;
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 6px;
        }

        .code-block {
            background-color: #f1f5f9;
            border-left: 3px solid #0284c7;
            padding: 10px 14px;
            font-family: "Courier New", Courier, monospace;
            font-size: 12px;
            color: #0f172a;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
        }

        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            font-size: 13px;
        }

        th,
        td {
            border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
            padding: 8px 12px;
            text-align: left;
        }

        th {
            background-color: #f8fafc;
            color: #0f172a;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .badge {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 2px 6px;
            font-size: 11px;
            font-weight: 600;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }

        .badge-normal {
            background-color: #dcfce7;
            color: #15803d;
        }

        .badge-anomaly {
            background-color: #fee2e2;
            color: #b91c1c;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <div class="header">
        <h1>Real-Time Network Anomaly Detection System</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Technical Implementation & Architecture Summary</p>
    </div>

    <div class="meta-grid">
        <div class="meta-item"><strong>Project Type:</strong> Full-Stack ML Web Application</div>
        <div class="meta-item"><strong>ML Model:</strong> Random Forest Classifier</div>
        <div class="meta-item"><strong>Backend Protocol:</strong> FastAPI & WebSockets</div>
        <div class="meta-item"><strong>Frontend Framework:</strong> React (Vite) + Recharts</div>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
    <p>
        This project presents a real-time network security monitoring system capable of continuously inspecting incoming
        packet data streams, identifying statistical anomalies, and rendering live telemetric diagnostics on a web
        dashboard. By pairing a Scikit-Learn Machine Learning pipeline with asynchronous WebSocket streaming, the
        platform delivers zero-latency threat detection for security operators.
    </p>

    <h2>2. System Architecture</h2>
    <div class="code-block">
        [ Incoming Traffic Data ]
        │
        ▼
        [ FastAPI Backend ] ──► [ Random Forest Model ] ──► Inference (0: Normal / 1: Anomaly)
        │
        ▼ (WebSocket Stream: ws://localhost:8000/ws/traffic)
        [ React Dashboard ] ──► Real-Time Recharts Telemetry + Packet Audit Feed
    </div>

    <h2>3. Machine Learning & Feature Telemetry</h2>
    <p>The network classifier evaluates live packet features against a trained Random Forest model:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Sttl (Source Time to Live):</strong> Measures hop limits to detect route spoofing and network
            scanning.</li>
        <li><strong>Proto (Protocol Identifier):</strong> Maps connection channels (TCP, UDP, ICMP).</li>
        <li><strong>Sload (Source Load):</strong> Tracks bit-rate metrics to flag Denial of Service (DoS) volume surges.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Spkts / Dpkts:</strong> Monitors packet balance ratios across endpoints.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Core Dashboard Components</h2>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Component</th>
                <th>Technology</th>
                <th>Functionality</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Live Bandwidth Chart</strong></td>
                <td>Recharts / React</td>
                <td>Plots rolling source load (Sload) traffic over time.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Packet Inspection Feed</strong></td>
                <td>HTML5 / CSS</td>
                <td>Displays real-time packet logs with color-coded threat badges.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Stream Service</strong></td>
                <td>FastAPI / WebSockets</td>
                <td>Pushes JSON-encoded predictions every second.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>5. Status Summary</h2>
    <p>
        Sample output status rendered by the real-time classification engine during evaluation:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Standard TCP Handshake Stream — <span class="badge badge-normal">NORMAL</span></li>
        <li>Elevated UDP Packet Rate Burst — <span class="badge badge-anomaly">ANOMALY</span></li>
    </ul>

</body>

</html>